{
  "dom_id": "step-e2282",
  "name": "Example: Approximating Ratios by Rounding to the Nearest Hundred",
  "problem": "The following table shows the number of boys and girls in a school.\n\n| Boys | Girls |\n| --- | --- |\n| $441$ | $569$ |\n\nRounding the given values to the nearest hundred, determine the approximate ratio of the number of boys to the total number of students (boys and girls).",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the number of boys and girls by rounding to the nearest hundred.\n\n- Number of boys: $441 \\longrightarrow 400$\n\n- Number of girls: $569 \\longrightarrow 600$\n\nThus, the total number of students is approximately $400 + 600 = 1,000.$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of boys to the total number of students is approximately\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{400}{1,000} \\, .\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $100$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{400 \\div 100}{1,000 \\div 100} = \\dfrac{4}{10}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4 \\div 2}{10 \\div 2} = \\dfrac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of boys to the total number of students is approximately $\\dfrac{2}{5}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
